# Purpose

This document defines the state engineering standards for the hubIO platform.

Its purpose is to establish clear ownership, predictable behavior, and sustainable boundaries for application state across the product so that interfaces remain understandable, scalable, and reliable as the platform grows.

---

# Scope

This standard defines:

* State philosophy
* State ownership
* State boundaries
* State consistency
* State synchronization
* State governance

It intentionally excludes framework-specific state libraries, component implementation, and data-fetching mechanics, which are defined by their respective Engineering Standards.

---

# Constitutional Interpretation

This document extends the hubIO Engineering Constitution.

It applies constitutional engineering principles to application state, ensuring state remains predictable, explicit, and aligned with the long-term architecture of the platform.

